## Quick Checklist for State Management

When writing React state updates, always ask:

- [ ] Am I using functional setState (`setState(prev => ...)`)?
- [ ] Am I capturing the new state if I need it immediately?
- [ ] Am I avoiding direct references to state after setState?
- [ ] Do I need to persist this state change?
- [ ] Are all dependencies included in useCallback/useEffect?
- [ ] Am I combining multiple state updates into one when possible?
- [ ] **Could this function run in parallel with other state updates?**
- [ ] **Am I reading state inside or outside the updater function?**
- [ ] Am I handling errors in async operations?

